Third-party content in the images (facts read from the layers)
  Base distribution: Alpine Linux (musl libc 1.1.24, BusyBox 1.31.1, bash 5.0.x, apk).
    front50, gate, orca   Alpine 3.11.7   43 apk packages   OpenJDK 11.0.5 (package 11.0.5_p10-r0)
    rosco                 Alpine 3.12.3   57 apk packages   OpenJDK 11.0.9 (package 11.0.9_p11-r0)
    clouddriver           Alpine 3.12.4   74 apk packages   OpenJDK 11.0.9 (package 11.0.9_p11-r0)
  JVM: OpenJDK 11 as packaged by Alpine ("IMPLEMENTOR=Alpine" in the JVM's release file,
    LIBC=musl, built for x86_64); licence GPL-2.0 with the Classpath exception (as recorded in
    the apk package metadata); the JDK's LICENSE and ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION files are in the image
    under /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk.
  Other packages whose recorded licence includes GPL or LGPL (from /lib/apk/db/installed):
    16 of 43 packages in front50/gate/orca, 20 of 57 in rosco, 32 of 74 in clouddriver. They
    include busybox (GPL-2.0-only), bash (GPL-3.0-or-later), readline, alsa-lib, freetype,
    libtasn1, pax-utils, apk-tools, and in clouddriver also git, util-linux, e2fsprogs, xz,
    gettext, wget, libidn2. Two packages (libxrender, libxtst) record the licence "custom";
    libssl/libcrypto 1.1 record "OpenSSL".
  clouddriver, further: Python (PYTHON_VERSION 3.7.10), AWS CLI 1.18.152, kubectl 1.18.10,
    Google Cloud SDK 313.0.1 (with its LICENSE at /opt/google-cloud-sdk), aws-iam-authenticator
    0.4.0, ecr-token v1.0.2 (versions from the image's environment variables; not checked
    file by file).
  rosco, further: HashiCorp Packer 1.6.6 and kustomize 3.8.5 (from the image's environment
    variables; not checked file by file).

Where the corresponding source of the distribution packages is available
  Each apk package record in /lib/apk/db/installed names its origin and the Alpine `aports`
  commit it was built from (field `c`). At such a commit the build recipe is at
    https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/raw/<commit>/<repository>/<origin>/APKBUILD
  (checked on 2026-11-14 for openjdk11 at ea4636f2a587561db565f796e436072868024cbf, community,
  and busybox at b8f92cf12ab6e48d1c3a7a0e590521581443e720, main). The recipe lists the source
  archives; Alpine's source mirror is https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/<v3.11|v3.12>/
  (busybox-1.31.1.tar.bz2 present for both). The OpenJDK source is the upstream tag
  jdk-11.0.9-ga / jdk-11.0.5-ga of https://github.com/openjdk/jdk11u (both tags resolve); the
  binary packages are still served at https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/<v3.11|v3.12>/
  (openjdk11-jre-headless 11.0.5_p10-r0 and 11.0.9_p11-r0 checked).
  This repository does not host the source of these packages. What would make a source
  archive possible without further research: for each image, the list of (package, version,
  aports commit) from the apk database (scripts/inventory-spinnaker.py --json writes it), the
  APKBUILD at that commit, and the tarballs named by `source=` in it, saved and published next
  to the images. That has not been done.

These images are from 2021 and receive no updates: the JVM, the libraries and OpenSSL 1.1.1
in them are unmaintained and should be assumed to have known vulnerabilities. They exist to
reproduce the behaviour of Spinnaker 1.25.4 in tests; do not run them with real credentials
or on exposed networks.
